#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-03.png", width: 420pt), 74.5pt, 138pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.84pt, 804pt, "3 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 81.96pt, "1.")
  #line-at(88.8pt, 81.96pt, "Introduction  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(106.2pt, 109.56pt, "The intersection of global warming and industrialization has catalyzed an urgent need ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 137.16pt, "for sustainable sources of clean water and energy [1]. Membrane technologies, particularly ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 164.76pt, "those utilizing highly hydrophobic, superhydrophobic, and self-cleaning membranes, are ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 192.36pt, "recognized as a sustainable and eco-friendly solution to tackle water and energy scarcity issues ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 219.96pt, "[1]. These membranes offer several benefits over other approaches, including flexibility, ease ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 247.56pt, "of use, and adaptability [2, 3]. The performance of membranes in membrane distillation (MD) ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 275.16pt, "is heavily influenced by their surface characteristics, particularly their wettability. These unique ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 302.76pt, "membranes play a crucial role in enhancing vapor flux and successfully combating issues such ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 330.36pt, "as wetting, scaling, and fouling [4]. When used in the desalination process, hydrophobic ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 357.96pt, "membranes come into contact with heated saline water (typically between 50 to 80°C) on the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 385.56pt, "feed side, making them an indispensable component in this transformative and sustainable ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 413.16pt, "technology [5, 6]. The temperature difference at the membrane prompts rapid evaporation at ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 440.76pt, "the interface between the membrane and the saline water. The vapor then diffuses through the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 468.36pt, "membrane's pores and condenses on the cooler side. The hydrophobic nature of the membrane ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 495.96pt, "prevents saline water from passing across, allowing only vapor to be transported [7-9]. This ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 523.56pt, "process effectively separates the volatile components (water) from the non-volatile ones (salts) ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 551.16pt, "in the heated saline solution. As a phase-change-based desalination method, MD is particularly ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 578.76pt, "effective for desalinating or concentrating brines with salinity levels exceeding the limits of ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 606.36pt, "reverse osmosis (~80")
  #line-at(174pt, 606.36pt, "ௗ")
  #line-at(176.4pt, 606.36pt, "g")
  #line-at(182.4pt, 606.36pt, "ௗ")
  #line-at(184.8pt, 606.36pt, "kg")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(196.92pt, 601.8pt, "-1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(203.64pt, 606.36pt, ") [10, 11]. Owing to its theoretical 100% rejection of non-volatile ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 633.96pt, "substances and reduced sensitivity to feed concentration, MD is deliberated a capable way for ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 661.56pt, "achieving zero liquid discharge when compared with crystallization technology [12-14]. MD ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 689.16pt, "desalination units have a straightforward design that does not require costly materials or high-")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 716.76pt, "pressure equipment, making it an accessible solution for providing drinking water in rural and ")
]

