  #line-at(70.8pt, 302.76pt, "features (roughness from 417 nm to 756 nm; average pore size in the range of 0.132 μm and ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 330.36pt, "0.226 μm) (Fig. 2). While the VIPS procedure, like other phase inversion methods, can achieve ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 357.96pt, "various morphologies like porous, dense, symmetric, or asymmetric ones, its distinctive ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 385.56pt, "capability to regulate the phase inversion rate effectively and membrane morphology offers a ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 413.16pt, "superior opportunity for precise customization compared to alternative phase inversion ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 440.76pt, "techniques [63]. ")
  #line-at(106.2pt, 468.36pt, "Membranes were characterized by a spheroid, symmetric nodular structure typical for ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 495.96pt, "VIPS membranes [64]. Nodular morphology, also referred to as granular or spherulitic ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 523.56pt, "structure, is a prevalent form observed in membranes produced through VIPS. Typically ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 551.16pt, "composed of semi-crystalline and crystalline polymers, this structure is consistently present ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 578.76pt, "across the entire cross-section of the generated membrane material. The slower intake rate of ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 606.36pt, "the non-solvent (water vapor) in VIPS promotes polymer crystallization over liquid-liquid ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 633.96pt, "demixing (L-L) [65-67]. Furthermore, this process sustains the cast film within the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 661.56pt, "crystallization region without being influenced by L-L phase separation. Consequently, this ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 689.16pt, "phenomenon results in the development of a granular structure and solid sphere, which extends ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 716.76pt, "throughout the overall cross-section of the material (Fig. 2, S2). Formation of such morphology ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 744.36pt, "is often associated with the gelation induced by crystallization [68] or when the critical ")
]

