  #line-at(106.32pt, 137.28pt, "Recalescence process, due to its very short duration time, is not easy to study both ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 164.88pt, "theoretically and experimentally [84]. However, we know that this process contains two stages: ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 192.48pt, "nucleation and growth of ice crystals. To get deeper into this process, we compared temperature ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 220.08pt, "profiles of the freezing process of the studied droplets (Fig. 8). ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.92pt, 525.6pt, "Fig. 8.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(106.8pt, 525.6pt, " Recorded profiles of temperature changes during the freezing process for the ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 541.44pt, "investigated membranes.  ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 569.28pt, "Obtained profiles (Fig. 8) are typical for the freezing process (see for example [84]). It is seen ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 596.88pt, "that the modifications performed in this study enhance the rate of droplet freezing compared to ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 624.48pt, "pure PVDF. From the profiles we determined two temperatures characterizing the process of ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 652.08pt, "recalescence, namely crystallization temperature and phase change temperature (see Fig.1 in ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 679.68pt, "[84]). We found a new and interesting relationship (Fig. 9), namely LEP, although not correlated ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 707.28pt, "with recalescence time, is linearly related to the phase change temperature.  ")
]

