  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(106.32pt, 82.08pt, "The motivation was to generate appropriate hydrophobic separation materials with long-")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 109.68pt, "lasting high wetting resistance and transport features to reduce the problem of hampering the ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 137.28pt, "mainstream implementation of MD [4]. In Fig. 12, it is visible that physically and chemically ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 164.88pt, "modified membranes possessed improved transport features referred to the pristine PVDF ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 192.48pt, "material. However, the chemical modification has been more beneficial and shows higher ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 220.08pt, "improvement in the water transport properties (flux, permeance, and overall transport ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 247.68pt, "coefficient), ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(132.96pt, 247.68pt, "i.e.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(147.6pt, 247.68pt, ", for the PVDF_Ch01 the enhancement at the lowest and the highest driving ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 275.28pt, "force was equal to 2.4 and 3.6 times, respectively. For the membrane PVDF_Ch02 these ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 302.88pt, "changes were equal to 1.6 and 2.0 times for the driving forces of 62.3 ± 3.9 mbar and 475.6 ± ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 330.48pt, "27.6 mbar, respectively (Fig. 12 and Table 3). Such profound improvement was a consequence ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 358.08pt, "of the attachment of hydrophilic modifiers that promote the transport of water by working as a ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 385.68pt, "“sponge”, as well as generating more rough surfaces on the membrane surface. It is essential ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 413.28pt, "that not only the significant transport upgrading was achieved but also the wetting resistance ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 440.88pt, "under high hydrostatic pressure (>11.4")
  #line-at(254.76pt, 440.88pt, "ௗ")
  #line-at(257.16pt, 440.88pt, "bar) without compromising vapor transport was ensured ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 468.48pt, "(Table 1). On the other hand, the improvement for membranes filled with 1-adamantanamine ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 496.08pt, "in the PVDF-matrix was slightly less significant. The enhancement of the transport features was ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 523.68pt, "in the 1.2 – 1.6 time range, depending on the driving forces (Table 3). The important influence ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 551.28pt, "of the amine moieties inside and outside the membrane material has been confirmed. A similar ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 578.76pt, "finding has been presented by Kyoungjin An and co-workers [39], who demonstrated that the ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 606.36pt, "incorporation of CNT-modifiers led to the formation of hierarchical structures with both nano ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 633.96pt, "and micro-scale roughness. These structures minimized boundary layer formation, enhancing ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 661.56pt, "the driving force in CNT-modified membranes. Moreover, the Roy et al. [87] presented that the ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 689.16pt, "addition of CNT with the carboxylic functional group into the polymeric matrix alters the ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 716.76pt, "hydrophilic–hydrophobic interaction between water moisture and the membrane surface and ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 744.36pt, "offers a supplementary pathway for improved transport of water vapor up to 51.5% when ")
]

