#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.08pt, 804pt, "45 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(106.32pt, 82.08pt, "Membrane stability and durability  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(106.32pt, 109.68pt, "The Hansen Solubility Parameters were assessed to control the stability of the ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 137.28pt, "membranes, and further tests were conducted to check their durability. These tests were applied ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 164.88pt, "to understand the influence of the AGMD process with VOCs on the features of membrane ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 192.48pt, "materials. Each membrane underwent five tests, each lasting at least 50 hours. The permeate ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 220.08pt, "flux, WCA, and roughness were precisely checked after each test. The results revealed ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 247.68pt, "membrane stability (Fig. 16). ")
  #line-at(106.32pt, 275.28pt, "However, it is worth noting that minor variations in stability were noticed between the ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 302.88pt, "pristine PVDF and the modified samples. The chemically modified samples (PVDF_Ch01 and ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 330.48pt, "PVFD_Ch02) exhibited more excellent resistance. A significant 25% reduction in transport ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 358.08pt, "properties for the unmodified PVDF between the first and last tests was noticed. In contrast, the ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 385.68pt, "permeate flux reduction for the PVDF_Ch01 and PVDF_Ch02 materials was merely 9% and ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 413.28pt, "6%, respectively. Moreover, the differences in contact angle ranged from 5% for the modified ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 440.88pt, "membranes to 8% for PVDF. A positive note is that the roughness parameters showed only ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 468.48pt, "negligible changes, remaining below 5% for all the investigated membranes. These findings ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 496.08pt, "confirm that, although a slight drop in transport was detected, the extended testing did not affect ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 523.68pt, "the grafted layer or the highly hydrophobic nature of the PVDF-based membranes. The high ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 551.28pt, "stability of the grafted layer in the case of PVDF_Ch02 has been additionally confirmed by the ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 578.76pt, "FTIR and SEM of the membranes used in the stability tests (Fig. 16 C, D). In addition, the ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 606.36pt, "stable WCA and roughness values unequivocally demonstrate the exceptional stability of the ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 633.96pt, "covalent modification.  ")
]

